obs THE FALL REACHED FURTHER THAN THE SIX. `unheard_guard` then reddened at a number it spells outright, and the reading had moved in the RIGHT direction: unnamed_choirs 12 -> 11, elder_reach_gap 2 -> 6. Proven by stashing this lap and re-running the scan on the elder tree, both ways.
obs THE CHAIN IS TWO HOPS AND IT IS THE LEVERAGE THE HEADER CLAIMS. `tools/g/glow_connector_seam_witness.rish` is an accrete shim whose whole body runs `tools/gen/chapter/glow_connector_seam_witness.rish`, which names `tools/gen/chapter/glow_hygiene_pin.rish` -- a choir singing six. Gathering ONE shim carried a six-guard choir into the heard set two hops down. The list diff names exactly that one path.
obs A WITNESS THAT SPELLS A MOVING NUMBER REDS ON CORRECT WORK. This is GRASS's own finding of this evening, one room over, and here it is a witness rather than a control: two asserts pinned unnamed_choirs=12 and unnamed_choir_ceiling=12, so lowering the population reddened the guard. Both lowered to 11 with the delta checked from both sides, in the file's own recorded-move convention. Whether the assert should read a FORM rather than a value is Grass's question and stays Keaton's.
obs AGAINST MYSELF: I edited tracked files while the cold pass ran, and the card asks a lap to hold still. It closed `tree_moved=yes` as it should. The hot pass after `git add` is the one measuring the tree this commit ships, and it is what I claim on.
obs NOT MINE, CARRIED FORWARD: the cold pass's three reds are `stash_record` (this seat's peer parked 16-plus stash entries), `standing_equipment` (`roster_broken` on an untracked run-card row `ran self_matching_assert 20260909.154933 absent` naming a guard absent from the tree and from the roster), and `unheard_guard`, which was mine and is closed above.
obs STILL YOURS, unchanged from my elder block: `?&` and `?|` in the closed pronunciation table; leading-zero syntax; decimal and aura length bounds; what declares a desk's kind (%532's fourth kind).
obs FOUND, NOT TAKEN: 57 further Glow witnesses read `unclocked` rather than `unheard` -- `tools/p/parity_ch01.rish` names every one and no roster row reaches it. A second choir over that list would be a second loom watching one lantern. The answer is a tier for the parity runner, it costs build time, and witness_reach_scan's own header already names it as Keaton's word.
